	)
	(text "Fujiversal-Atari2600 - Rev0 (RP2040, fujivcs)\n\nRP2040 serves the 4K cart window: A0-A12 on GP2-14, D0-D7 on GP15-22, '245 DIR on GP26 (low = cart drives),\nLED on GP25, 2 MB W25Q16 flash (pico-sdk board fujivcs).  The RP2040 is NOT 5V tolerant, so every bus\nline crosses a 74LVC245A powered at 3.3V (5V-tolerant inputs, 3.3V outputs meet the NMOS bus's TTL VIH):\nU3 A0-A7 and U4 A8-A12 fixed A->B, U5 D0-D7 with DIR = GP26 (pulled high: never drives until told).\nESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 runs FujiNet (fujiversal-atari2600) and is the USB host of the RP (CDC, VID 0xCafe);\nS3 IO4/IO5 force RP RUN/QSPI_SS (1k, active low) so the S3 can reset / BOOTSEL the RP.\nRESET resets both chips (back to the browser).  USB-C: power + CP2102N UART bridge for flashing the S3.\nPower: console +5V (edge 23) and USB VBUS diode-OR -> AP63203 3.3V buck; nothing else touches the edge 5V.\nEdge: pins 1-12 on the console-FRONT face (B.Cu), 13-24 on the component face (F.Cu, console REAR)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
